{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Rectifier bridges",
  "exampleId": "block-rectifiers",
  "description": "The diode bridge turns both halves of the 10 V, 50 Hz sine positive, so its output averages 2 · 10 V / π = 6.37 V. The thyristor bridge is fired 5 ms, or 90°, into each half-cycle, so it passes only the second quarter of each half and averages 10 V / π · (1 + cos 90°) = 3.18 V.",
